# Format after edit

After creating or updating any file, **format it before marking the task complete**.

## Workflow

1. Make the required code or doc changes.
2. Format every file you touched in that task.
3. Fix any formatting-related linter or editor diagnostics on those files.

## How to format

Prefer an automated formatter when available:

```bash
# Project format script (if defined)
pnpm run format

# Prettier (if installed or configured)
npx prettier --write path/to/changed-file.ts
```

If no formatter is configured, format manually and match the surrounding file:

- 2-space indentation
- Trailing newline at end of file
- No trailing whitespace on lines
- Consistent semicolon style within the file
- Import groups and blank lines per the ES6 coding standards rule

## Scope

Applies to all edited files: TypeScript, JavaScript, JSON, Markdown, CSS, and config files.

Never leave edited files unformatted when finishing a task.
